   "id": "news-101",
   "title": "U of I-Led Study Finds Ongoing Evolution in Tasmanian Devils’ Response to Transmissible Cancer",
   "date": "2021-05-26",
   "body": "University of Idaho researchers partnered with other scientists from the U.S. and Australia to study the evolution of Tasmanian devils in response to a unique transmissible cancer. “Our work suggests that maintaining genetic diversity across a wide set of functionally important genes is critical to make sure Tasmanian devils are able to adapt to transmissible cancers and other threats to their survival,” said Dept. of Biological Sciences Associate Professor Paul Hohenlohe.",
   "image": "content/assets/news/tasmanian-devil-menna-jones-crop.jpg",
   "source_url": "https://www.iids.uidaho.edu/news.php?newsid=101",
